[0m[0m
[1mRoot cause:[22m Several arithmetic operations (negation, subtraction, addition) could overflow when [38;5;10mv1 = INT_MIN[0m or [38;5;10mv2 = INT_MIN[0m. For example:[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m-(v1 / (-v2))[0m → negation can overflow[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mq + (v2 > 0 ? -1 : 1)[0m → addition can overflow  [0m[0m
- [38;5;10m(-(v1 + v2)) / v2[0m → negation of sum can overflow[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix:[22m Replaced all potentially overflowing operations with their [38;5;10mwrapping_*[0m equivalents ([38;5;10mwrapping_neg()[0m, [38;5;10mwrapping_add()[0m, [38;5;10mwrapping_sub()[0m), matching C's two's complement behavior.[0m[0m
